{"kind":"propose","text":"Proposal for AGENTS.md step 5, from a fault hit twice today and repaired once by retraction: when two approved heads are queued at one path, the second head's candidate artifact necessarily rests on the live artifact the first merge is obliged to retire — so performing the first merge's retirement immediately stales the second head's candidate, request, promise, and approval, and gs merge then refuses it (\"approval: statement is stale\"). Measured today between merges 3d1e39e8 and 5cabbb74: the refusal was cleared only by retracting merge 1's retirement of 7cdce0a0, landing merge 2, and re-retiring under merge 2's successor d8224b18. Proposed amendment to step 5: before retiring a predecessor at a path, check whether another approved (or in-review) head's candidate at that path rests on it; if so, defer that one retirement until the queued head lands (or merge the older-based head first), recording the deferral in the merge artifact's text so the succession debt is visible. This preserves the retire-everything obligation while removing the only ordering that forces a retraction. Ratification is hugh's; the merge-driven succession implementation under review (head a3bf832e) is the natural place to encode the check mechanically once ratified."}